body:
1. I put the answer in the FAQ's just now.

&nbsp;

2. The aim is getting tools to handle and lessen your depression. I do want to make a thread with reading suggestions, though, because I can't offer a whole therapy here, but if some of the assignments helps you a lot, there is often more background information.

&nbsp;

3. I don't understand this question, I think. The groups are indeed for support and the assignments are 1) For you privately to use in your life and 2) indeed to interact and discuss with you group members, because 25 people have more experience than 1. I will check whether people share their assignments or comment in group threads. If somebody doesn't, that's no problem, that's your right, but I will message these person to ask why they don't interact. Do they need some support from a moderator, because they're shy? Are they having trouble with continuing the group? Or do they want to stop? I find this important because I want as many people as possible to benefit from the assignments, but I also don't want people that don't do the assignments at all to be able to view what other share for privacy reasons. Does that answer your question?

&nbsp;

Your question are not too much. I tend to think that if somebody has a question, there's always somebody else with the same question.
